meta {
  name: 04 Get Sample History
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/samples/{{sampleId}}/history
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  The sample's status-MOVEMENT log (§A.10.5), newest first, for the Audit
  Trail UI. Each row carries `action`, `fromStatus`, `toStatus`, optional
  `reason` / `notes` / `attachmentUrl`, and `changedBy` (raw `Person.id`).

  Only rows where the sample's status actually moved from one real status to
  another are returned (`fromStatus` non-null and different from `toStatus`).
  The underlying `accession_status_history` table also has non-movement rows
  — the system-written `generate` row (sample created from the order,
  `fromStatus = null`, no prior status to move FROM) and no-status-change
  actions (`assign-barcode`, `update` notes, both written with `fromStatus
  === toStatus`) — these are real audit facts kept in the table, but this
  endpoint filters them out since they aren't lifecycle movement. A sample
  still sitting at NEW with nothing done to it yet returns `[]`.

  Each row is also enriched with `actorName` (the `changedBy` person's full
  name) and `actorRole` (their CURRENT role name at the caller's active
  branch, via `UserBranchProfile` → `AuthRole` — not a snapshot of the role
  held at the time of the action, since that isn't captured anywhere in this
  codebase today). Both are `null` if unresolved, e.g. a person with no
  active profile at this branch.
}
